      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Pseudoaneurysms (PA) in the arterial supply of the breast are quite rare and mostly iatrogenic secondary to biopsies. Breast PAs after blunt trauma is even rarer. In this paper, a case of breast PAs secondary to blunt trauma and its percutaneous treatment using human thrombin injection and after N-butyl cyanoacrylate is presented."
